// x° (postfix) scopes to its nearest @ loop; dies when that loop ends.
// After loop-1 ends, x is gone; >> x below is a compile-time "undefined variable" error.
// Use °x (prefix) when the variable should survive past the loop.

// x° anchors AT loop-1; after loop-1 ends, x is gone; loop-2 starts fresh
@ i:1..3 { x° += i }
@ j:1..3 { x° += j }
>> x ¶
